# NFL Player Contact Detection — swarm final solution

Task: binary contact detection (player-player + player-Ground) at 10 Hz; metric **MCC**.
Final artifact: `submission.csv` (463,243 rows, `contact_id,contact`).

## Solution summary
Two separate models (pair-contact and ground-contact), shared 5-fold **GroupKFold by game_key**
(`folds.csv`, seed 42), then temporal smoothing and joint threshold calibration.

### 1. Tracking + temporal features (rigel_delta)
`build_track_features.py` / `make_data.py`:
- pair kinematics (distance, dx/dy, relative velocity, closing speed, time-to-contact,
  direction/orientation differences, team flags), lags/leads and centered rolling
  min/mean of distance & kinematics (numba), per-step neighbourhood counts.
- separate ground feature set (player kinematics + temporal).
- LightGBM per subtype -> `oof_pair.parquet`, `oof_ground.parquet`, `testpred_*.parquet`.

### 2. Tracking+helmet pair model (rigel_delta)
`train_pair_helmet.py`: the tracking features merged with helmet-bbox geometry features and
nearest-neighbour context produced by achernar_sigma -> `oof_pair_h.parquet`.

### 3. Ground level-2 stacker (rigel_delta)
`ground_stack.py`: LightGBM on base ground probabilities (rigel tracking, achernar v1/fusion,
castor tab/video) + per-series lags/leads/rolling + context -> `ground_oof_stack_r.parquet`,
`ground_test_stack_r.parquet`.

### 4. Consensus blender (rigel_delta, `final_blend.py`)
- Pair models: rigel tracking, rigel tracking+helmet, achernar v1, achernar v2 (weights
  searched on OOF, step 0.1 + local refine, maximizing pair MCC).
- Ground models: rigel ground stacker, achernar ground fusion, achernar ground v2,
  castor ground video (weights searched on OOF).
- Centered rolling-mean smoothing per series: pair window 3 (~0.3 s), ground window 15 (~1.5 s).
- Pair/ground thresholds tuned jointly on OOF (joint MCC), then for the submitted file the
  **test thresholds are rate-matched** to the OOF-optimal positive rate (pair 1.15%, ground 4.50%).
  This corrects for the probability shrinkage of fold-averaged test predictions
  (raw OOF thresholds under-predict the test set badly).

OOF (shared folds): pair MCC ≈ 0.7669, ground MCC ≈ 0.7388, **joint MCC ≈ 0.7607**.

## Files
- `submission.csv` — final predictions (rate-matched thresholds).
- `final_blend.py` — consensus blender / weight search / smoothing / thresholds.
- `postprocess_search.py` — numba temporal smoothing + MCC/threshold search.
- `build_track_features.py`, `make_data.py` — feature pipeline.
- `finish_models.py`, `train_pair_helmet.py`, `ground_stack.py` — base model training.
- `quick_eval.py` — fast OOF MCC evaluation.

Inputs expected next to the workspace directories:
`workspaces/rigel_delta/*`, `workspaces/achernar_sigma/*`, `workspaces/castor_alpha/*`
(see blackboard messages for provenance of the shared features/predictions).

## Reproduce / evaluate
```
pyenv shell sis-black
cd workspaces/rigel_delta
python make_data.py            # build tracking features
python finish_models.py        # tracking-only pair/ground LGBM
python train_pair_helmet.py    # tracking+helmet pair LGBM
python ground_stack.py         # ground level-2 stacker
python final_blend.py          # weights + smoothing + thresholds -> submission_consensus*.csv
```
